  "methodology": "Other",
  "methodology_other": "Data were collected from the 2006 Population and Housing Census, Geographic, Population & Demographic Data (GeoPoDe), Nigeria, U.S. Census Bureau, 2019, Subnational Population Estimates, the Annual Abstract of Statistics Vol. 2, 2017 from the National Bureau of Statistics, the Annual Abstract of Statistics, Vol. 1, from the National Bureau of Statistics, the Displacement Tracking Matrix Nigeria Baseline Assessment Round 26 from the International Organization for Migration, and the Multiple Indicator Cluster Survey 2016-17. Census Bureau staff altered boundaries and modified the statistical data as detailed in the Metadata tab of the tabular data.",
  "name": "nigeria-subnational-boundaries-and-tabular-data",
  "notes": "The geodatabase contains boundaries for the national and first- and second- order administrative divisions, aligned to the Large Scale International Boundaries dataset from the U.S. Department of State. The feature classes are suitable for linking to the attribute data provided.\r\n\r\nThe tabular data contain total population for 2006 (census) and 2019 (population estimates), as well as five-year age group and sex, and information relating to households, nationality, information and communication technology, migration and displacement, health, and poverty. ",
